# whetstone

Root invariants for the whetstone codebase. Picked up by `find_all_sdd` and
surfaced to the model in the task prompt when `set_repo_root` points at
the whetstone checkout itself; read by humans and Claude Code as the
authoritative architectural contract.

whetstone is the **M5-era research fork of luxe** (forked from luxe HEAD).
Its mandate is to re-open, under the 96 GB M5 Max memory envelope, the
decisions luxe/deluxe closed under the old 36 GB M1 cap, and to bank any
reproducible improvement over the luxe champion. Unlike luxe (mono-only) and
deluxe (dense-only, mono-only), whetstone is **permitted to run multi-model
pipelines** — specifically the sanctioned planner/builder split under
`src/whetstone/agents/pipeline/**`. This is the single deliberate
architectural divergence from luxe; everything else stays a faithful fork.

Sourced from `lessons.md` postmortems, the approved plan
(`~/.claude/plans/soft-meandering-gadget.md`), and durable user auto-memory.

## Must
- temp=0.0 in production fixture configs (determinism; pinned by luxe variance probe)
- Establish a fresh `acceptance/baseline_m5_96gb/` (champion at the 96 GB cap, 3× for
  determinism) as the comparison denominator; every track cites deltas vs that baseline,
  never old-M1 or auto-cap absolutes
- Memory envelope is **96 GB** (`iogpu.wired_limit_mb=98304`, oMLX `max_model_memory:"96GB"`,
  `max_process_memory:"110GB"`); a variant aborts rather than exceed it
- Multi-model pipelines are permitted ONLY under `src/whetstone/agents/pipeline/**`; the
  builder pass reuses `agents/loop.py:run_agent` and `single.py:_build_full_tool_surface`
  unchanged for tool-surface parity (no forked loop)
- Per-track / per-role model selection is permitted (planner ≠ builder); record the roster
  and write results under `acceptance/<track>_m5_96gb/`
- All prompt strings (mono AND planner) go through `src/whetstone/agents/prompts.py` registry
- Pin `--work-dir ~/.whetstone/bench-workspace` for bench runs (random tempdir leaks into prompts)
- `oMLX` `idle_timeout_seconds: 1800` by default; raise to 3600 (or pin `--keep-loaded`) during
  pipeline runs so the planner is not evicted between Pass 1 and Pass 2
- `--keep-loaded` for bench mode (post-run unload fires by default); `unload_all_loaded()` MUST
  fire at every variant cleanup boundary, including on bailout, so a resident model never
  poisons the next fixture's baseline
- Read the shared, read-only fixture cache at `~/.luxe/fixture-cache/` (shared with luxe for
  cross-repo delta comparability — do NOT repoint to `~/.whetstone/`)
- Upstream any harness/bench fix discovered here to luxe; the pipeline package is the only
  sanctioned divergence and must not silently fork shared logic

## Must not
- Read `origin/<branch>` in offline-cache repos (stale-ref trap; use local ref or sidecar regrade)
- Use MoE Instruct-2507 model family (long-context fabrication, skips optional tool calls)
- Use `--no-verify`, `--no-gpg-sign`, or other hook-skip flags
- Force-push to `main` or `master`
- Run two model rosters concurrently (≥80 GB peak; sequential bake-offs only)
- Compare whetstone runs against luxe/deluxe acceptance JSON collected on other hardware/caps

## Owns
- src/whetstone/**

## Forbids
- src/swarm/**
- src/micro/**
- src/phased/**
